{
  "_": "money's screenshots (.github/screens/apps.md; which phones it is on is flake.nix's list, `publish`): its server is server.sh, seeded up to the run's day (DEMO_DAY), signed in to as `user`, who goes by `name`. `walk`: the phones' and the larger screens' (each a list), walked inside the app from a new install (ui/docs/shots.md, \"In the App\"): `welcome`, the first run's page a new install opens on; then signed in through the first run (`welcome.next`, the server's address typed into `welcome.typed` — `{server}` is the run's — `welcome.check`), landing on the budget; and every shot after reached by tapping from where the last left it, each step naming an element by its id (ui/docs/shots.md: `tab:budget`, `budget.row:dining-out`, `shell.new-transaction`; a shot's `<id>.tree.txt` lists them). `welcome` is taken every way at the start; the rest is walked whole once a way (light, then dark; on the iPad then dark and light on its side), the app reset in it between walks (`ArkHost.shotsReset`), the sign-in's steps (`signIn`) on the first walk alone. A category and a transaction are opened in the platform's way: on a phone Category Details' sheet and the transaction's form; on a larger screen the inspector (Transaction Details shown first). `wide`: the wide windows' one walk, by the same ids in the same order on all three (.github/screens/apps.md, \"The wide windows\"): the desktop's iced window (app-desktop.sh, ui/rust/shots: signed in straight back from the run's dev server), the browser's page (app-web.sh, web-shots.js: the page published as the demo, `web.demo`) and the Mac's own window (app-mac.sh: the demo's household, `mac`), each at `window` (`scale` the desktop's pixels), light then dark, each step taken inside the app by its id (`ark_app::shots`: ArkHost's on the Mac, as the iPhone's walk; the page's `window.arkShots`; the desktop's window's). The demo of the Mac and the browser is on the run's day (DEMO_DAY), else `today`. What one platform alone can do is a narrow addition, said by `on`: a shot or a step `on` some of `desktop`, `web` and `mac` is taken there alone (the desktop's vim keys; the browser's transient parts, each opened in a page of its own by its address, `query`, as arkui-web reads it). `mac` is the Mac's own launch arguments, and `welcome` its first run's page, opened with no demo before the walk.",
